            "title": "File handling",
            "text": "File handling means reading from and writing to files; it is essential for storing data permanently, beyond the end of the program."
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "Why do programs need file handling?",
            "explanation": "Variables are lost when a program ends; files keep data so it can be used again later."
          },
